&#x201C;Christina has spent her career turning relationships and creative ideas into meaningful business,&#x201D; said Made By All CEO Perice, who founded the company in 2017. &#x201C;She understands what brands need and how creators can deliver it without losing what makes them distinctive. Her experience will be invaluable as we expand our talent roster, strengthen our management team and create new opportunities for our clients.&#x201D;

Most recently, Tom served as Senior Director, Partnerships at creator-focused tech and licensing firm Spotter, where she developed creator content partnerships and secured business with entertainment clients including A24, Amazon MGM Studios and Focus Features.

Previously, she was Regional Vice President, Partnerships at Penske Media Corporation&#x2019;s Rolling Stone, overseeing West Coast business across entertainment, technology, gaming and other major categories. During her tenure, she launched the publication&#x2019;s Creators Issue in partnership with Meta.

Tom&#x2019;s career also includes roles at Entertainment Weekly, Billboard, Disney and Nickelodeon, with experience spanning television, digital, social, branded content and live events. She also recently led brand partnerships on a contract basis for women&#x2019;s sports marketing firm Trailblazing Sports Group. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

"The creator economy has evolved into a powerful business ecosystem, creating tremendous opportunities for talent, brands and the businesses that support them," said Tom. "Having had the privilege of working with Leanne for many years, I&#x2019;ve seen firsthand her vision for the industry and her ability to build meaningful opportunities for creators.

"I&#x2019;m incredibly excited to join her and the Made By All team, bringing my passion for the creator economy and extensive experience developing strategic brand partnerships to help strengthen brand relationships, create new avenues for growth and build lasting value for our talent and the business.&#x201D;

Earlier this year, Made By All launched a production arm , Made By Us Studios , with former Range partner Tanya Cohen named co-CEO to lead the business alongside Perice and President of Production Nic Stanish, who also leads marketing content studio Made By Us .

The BAFTA Awards is losing its long-standing headline sponsor.

Brit mobile and internet provider EE, which has sponsored the U.K.'s biggest film event for almost 30 years, is ending its partnership with the awards following the next ceremony in February 2027. The decision was driven by EE's "business strategy," according to the British Academy, which said it was first told about the move at the end of 2025. Related Stories Pink Announces 2027 Sphere Residency in Las Vegas

&#x201C;2027 will mark the 30th year of the EE BAFTA Film Awards," said a BAFTA spokesperson. "After a long-standing, successful and trusted partnership, EE advised us more than a year ago that it would not be renewing its support of the Film Awards beyond the end of the current contract which runs to the end of 2027, confirming that this decision is entirely driven by EE&#x2019;s business strategy." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The spokesperson added: "We are incredibly proud of what we have achieved together over three decades and are fully focused on delivering an exceptional EE BAFTA Film Awards in February, where we look forward to celebrating the very best in film with EE and audiences throughout the UK and world-wide.&#x201D;

EE first became title sponsor of the BAFTA awards in 2013, taking over from its sister company Orange, which started the relationship in 1998. Alongside being the chief sponsor of the event, it adds its name to the EE Rising Star Award. P&O Cruises, meanwhile, is the headline sponsor of the BAFTA TV Awards.

BAFTA is already in discussions with potential sponsors to take over for the 2028 film awards ceremony.
